# CLAUDE.me — Finca Libia Digital Concierge Guidelines

This document provides developer guidelines, design principles, commands, and code patterns for working with the **Finca Libia Private Digital Concierge** repository.

---

## 🛠️ Common Commands

### Development
- `npm run dev` — Start Vite development server (`http://localhost:5173`)
- `npm run build` — Build production bundle & PWA assets into `dist/`
- `npm run preview` — Locally preview the production build
- `npm run typecheck` — Run TypeScript type checking (`tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.app.json`)
- `npm run lint` — Run ESLint across the codebase (`eslint .`)

---

## 🎨 Design System & Philosophy

This application is built with a **Luxury Hospitality First** mindset ("Boutique Hotel × Editorial Magazine × Private Members Club").

### Core Aesthetic Rules
- **No Generic SaaS/Dashboard Aesthetics**: Avoid bright gradients, crowded card grids, generic icons, dense data tables, or "tech startup" UI elements.
- **Generous Whitespace & Restraint**: Prioritize single hero images, short editorial sentences, and large breathing room.
- **Color Palette Tokens** (defined in [`tailwind.config.js`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/tailwind.config.js)):
  - Base Background: `bg-ink-900` (`#1a1816`)
  - Primary Text / Headers: `text-ivory-50` (`#fdfcf9`) / `text-ivory-100` (`#f9f6ef`)
  - Subtext / Muted UI: `text-stone-400` / `text-stone-500` / `text-ink-700`
  - Accent / CTA: `text-champagne-400` / `bg-champagne-500`
  - Status Indicators: `text-olive-400`
- **Typography Guidelines**:
  - Headings & Editorial Quotes: `font-serif` (`Cormorant Garamond`) with font weights `font-light` or `font-normal` (e.g. `font-serif text-5xl font-light`).
  - Body & Micro-labels: `font-sans` (`Inter`) with tracked uppercase styling (e.g. `text-xs uppercase tracking-widest-2 text-stone-500`).
- **Animations**: Use the [`Reveal`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/src/components/Reveal.tsx) component for scroll-triggered entrance animations, and Tailwind custom keyframe animations (`animate-fade-up`, `animate-fade-in`).

