## 📁 Codebase Architecture

- [`src/App.tsx`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/src/App.tsx): Top-level component managing view state (`home`, `stay`, `explore`, `concierge`, `memories`, `itinerary`, `pre-arrival`, `checkout`), scroll listener, bottom navigation bar, and floating Concierge CTA button.
- [`src/views/`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/src/views/): Page components corresponding to each section of the app.
- [`src/components/`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/src/components/): Reusable UI primitives ([`Reveal.tsx`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/src/components/Reveal.tsx), [`BackButton.tsx`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/src/components/BackButton.tsx), [`FullScreenImage.tsx`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/src/components/FullScreenImage.tsx)).
- [`src/data/content.ts`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/src/data/content.ts): Centralized static data repository for property metadata, amenities, recommendations, stories, residents, itinerary steps, and checkout guidelines.
- [`src/types/index.ts`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/src/types/index.ts): Centralized TypeScript interface definitions.
- [`src/lib/supabase.ts`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/src/lib/supabase.ts): Client instance for Supabase API interactions.

---

## 🗄️ Database Integration & Supabase

The app operates as a single-tenant application without authentication (QR-code based access).

- **`concierge_requests` Table**: Stores requests sent via [`ConciergeView.tsx`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/src/views/ConciergeView.tsx).
- **`guestbook_entries` Table**: Stores memories submitted via [`CheckoutView.tsx`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/src/views/CheckoutView.tsx) and displayed in [`MemoriesView.tsx`](file:///Users/aryanchauhan/Downloads/guestbook-i/src/views/MemoriesView.tsx).
- **RLS Configuration**: Anonymous access (`anon`) is enabled for `SELECT` and `INSERT` operations (`USING (true)` / `WITH CHECK (true)`).

